UPDATE Students
SET State = 'Kentucky'
WHERE State = 'KY';

UPDATE modifies existing data in a table — it changes the values of one or more columns in rows that match a WHERE condition.

Syntax: UPDATE table SET column1 = value1, column2 = value2 WHERE condition;
Example: UPDATE Employees SET Salary = Salary * 1.1 WHERE Department = 'IT';
Without WHERE, every row in the table is updated.

